Package: linux-island
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Linux Island maintainers <linux-island@localhost>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), libxcb-cursor0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xkb1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxext6, libegl1, libgl1, libfontconfig1, libdbus-1-3, x11-xserver-utils
Recommends: wireplumber | pulseaudio-utils, libpulse0, libxss1, bluez
Description: dynamic-island style pill for the Linux desktop
 A small pill at the top of the screen (on one, several or all monitors)
 that shows what is playing in any MPRIS player with controls and a seek
 bar, pops up for volume, brightness, charger and Bluetooth/headphone
 changes, shows camera and microphone indicators, swoops into a clock and
 calendar card when every window is minimised, and turns into a clock
 screensaver when idle or locking.
 .
 Everything can be configured in the settings panel (Linux Island
 Settings). Works on X11 (and through XWayland); Qt 6 (PySide6) is bundled
 in /opt/linux-island and runs with any Python 3.10 - 3.15.
